<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Charles Emmanuel II, Duke of Savoy</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1634–1675</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Charles Emmanuel II was duke of Savoy from 1638 to 1675, succeeding as a child under the regency of his mother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christine-of-france">Christine of France</a>, who remained influential until her death in 1663. His reign saw the massacre of the Waldensians in 1655, known as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piedmontese-easter">Piedmontese Easter</a>, and much building in and around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turin">Turin</a>, including the Venaria Reale hunting palace. His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/victor-amadeus-ii">Victor Amadeus II</a> succeeded him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charles-emmanuel-ii-duke-of-savoy.jpg" alt="Charles Emmanuel II, Duke of Savoy" width="320" height="393" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Charles Dauphin · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ritratto_di_Carlo_Emanuele_II_di_Savoia..png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
